    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The U.S. military continues to invest in advanced technologies such as drones and unmanned aircraft, aiming for rapid development and deployment. The U.S. Army has successfully turned the Merops drone into a program of record, while the Lakota Connector and Specter drones are in development. The U.S. Navy is deploying carrier strike groups in the Western Pacific and Indian Ocean, conducting maritime security operations and humanitarian assistance missions. The U.S. Army is also modernizing the Bradley Fighting Vehicles with a new proposal from General Dynamics Land Systems. The SR-71 Blackbird could potentially be modified to reach Mach 4, with significant modifications and cost increase required. The U.S. Navy is also deploying forward-deployed destroyers and cruisers in transit, preparing for future deployments.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
